  "raw_label": "appellant_lost",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Murugan vs The District Collector on 31 January, 2024 Author: V.Bhavani Subbaroyan Bench: V.Bhavani Subbaroyan W.P(MD)No.18 Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated : 31.01.2024 Coram The Honourable Mrs.Justice V.Bhavani Subbaroyan W.P(MD)No.1890 of 2024 and W.M.P(MD)Nos.1903 and 1904 of 2024 Murugan ... -Vs- 1.The District Collector, Collectorate, Kanyakumari District at Nagercoil. 2.The Block Development Officer, Block Development Office, Thovalai Village Union, Kanyakumari District. 3.The Village President/Executive Officer, Sagayanagar Village Panchayat, Thovalai Village Union, Shanmugapuram Mathavalaayam Post, Kanyakumari District. ... Respon Prayer:- Writ Petition is filed under Article 226 of the Constituti India, praying for the issuance of a Writ of Certiorarified Mandamu for the records of the impugned order of the 3rd respondent in his 1/6 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis W.P(Md) Murugan vs The District Collector on 31 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/199812934/ 1 proceedings dated 30.12.2023 and quash the same as illegal and furt direct the respondents 1 to 3 herein to permit the petitioner to ru shop in the name and style Vaigai Broilers at Shop No. 1-37, Vellam Junction, Thovalai, Kanyakumari District. For Petitioner : Mr.S.Vashik Ali For Respondents : Mr.D.Gandhi Raj Spl. Govt. Pleader (for R1) Mr.K.S.Selvaganesan Addl. Govt. Pleader (for R2) Mr.Niranjan S.Kumar (for R3)",
    "facts": ". The subject matter property belongs to one Maniammal. After entering into a lease agreement dated 17.07.2020 with the said landlady, the petitioner was running a broiler shop in the name and style Vaigai Broilers in the subject matter property. While so, the landlady has tried to evict the petitioner and she refused to receive the rent. Hence, the petitioner has filed a civil suit in O.S.No.49 of 2022 and got interim injunction dated 03.11.2022 in I.A.No.2 of 2022. While so, the third respondent sent a notice dated 21.07.2023 and 01.08.2023 seeking explanation for running the above shop without any permission from the third respondent. Thereafter, the third respondent has passed a resolution No.126 dated 08.08.2023 to seal the petitioner's shop without providing any opportunity. Hence, he filed W.P(MD)No.28473 of 2023 and this Court vide order dated 04.12.2023, directed the third respondent to consider the representation of the petitioner within a period of four weeks. However, the third respondent has rejected the petitioner's representation vide impugned order dated 30.12.2023. Thereafter, the third respondent had affixed a notice on 04.01.2024 to seal the petitioner's shop on 05.01.2024.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
